Provides: redmine-mcp-server
Replaces: redmine-mcp-server (<< 2.4.1~)
Breaks: redmine-mcp-server (<< 2.4.1~)
Description: MCP server for Redmine project management
 Production-ready Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that connects
 AI assistants to Redmine issue tracking and project management.
 .
 Exposes a /mcp endpoint (default port 8000) with authentication,
 pagination, file management, and enterprise security features.
 .
 A compatible pydantic-core is bundled privately in
 /usr/lib/redmine-mcp-server/ and activated via the launcher's
 PYTHONPATH so no system packages are modified.

Package: mcprack-mcp-server-redmine
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 mcprack (>= 1.5.4),
 mcp-server-redmine (= ${binary:Version}),
Description: Registers Redmine MCP server into mcprack catalog
 Companion package for mcp-server-redmine. Installing it registers
 the redmine-mcp-server binary (stdio mode, non-OAuth auth only) as
 an available MCP server in the local mcprack instance; removing it
 unregisters it again.
